+
+
+`RenderPipelineDescriptor::ordered_fragment_primitives` opts into a limited raster-order-group
+fallback for devices without native fragment interlock. When the compiler returns the
+`OrderedFragmentPrimitives` dependency, direct and indexed single-sample, single-layer triangle lists run
+one primitive per render-pass instance with full memory dependencies. A single triangle retains
+all draw IDs; longer indexed lists retain base vertex and, for one instance, base instance.
+Other draws reading base IDs or primitive ID, indirect draws, meshes and tessellation are refused
+as `RuntimeGap::OrderedFragmentPrimitives`. This does not advertise native interlock or complete
+ROG support and can add a render pass for each primitive.
