+
+## PanVK idle command-pool memory
+
+PanVK retains at most two idle command pools per queue family (`spares.rs`). A pool
+returns only after its work completed or was never submitted; destruction happens outside
+the spare-list lock, and live or pending pools are never evicted. This releases the driver's
+per-pool TLS scratch allocations after a burst. The newest pools remain reusable; exceeding
+the bound can increase pool creation cost but does not change command results. Other drivers
+keep the historical maximum number of pools, including NVIDIA's destruction-hang workaround.
